    {
      "id": "code",
      "name": "Code Like It's 198x",
      "purpose": "Help people understand programming by making games on machines they can understand.",
      "headline": "Selected first programs build, change and reopen.",
      "assessment": "The four core routes are authored. Selected first-program workflows now have evidence for editing, rebuilding and reopening on macOS; the rest of the curriculum still needs content and learner acceptance.",
      "demonstrated": "Spectrum editing and recovery, C64 red/green PRG execution, Amiga red/green bootable disks and the NES edited-cartridge handoff have retained observations. The C64 starter and Amiga instructions were corrected during these checks.",
      "gap": "Uncoached understanding remains unobserved. Screen-reader use, touch, wider lesson review and deferred Windows/Linux manual walkthroughs remain open. One successful program does not establish a complete course.",
      "checkpoint": "Review the next NES lesson, \u201cLDA Is Not LET\u201d, against its running program: register explanation, predicted result and fault/repair task.",
      "checkpoint_reason": "This checks the transition from changing a colour to explaining how the machine stores and transfers a value.",
      "reviewed_on": "2026-10-19",
