      "id": "emu",
      "name": "Emu198x",
      "purpose": "Run historical machines accurately enough to inspect, explain and create with them.",
      "headline": "Named workflows run; broader usability remains open.",
      "assessment": "Selected browser and native paths execute the first programs. Results belong to their named model, release and host; native candidate acceptance and released-binary execution remain separate.",
      "demonstrated": "Released Emu198x 0.38.1 boots the selected A500 disks and runs the downloaded NTSC NES cartridge. The Spectrum macOS keyboard, listening and recovery checklists received user-reported acceptance; C64 browser PRG execution also passed.",
      "gap": "Other models and complete native input, sound and file workflows still need their own evidence. Windows/Linux manual checks are deferred. Hosted Spectrum evidence retention remains blocked; local success does not remove that blocker.",
